:: Vault [sugarcast] {"title":"03 / The Guest Beneath the Stairs"}
<<widget "comfortMeter">>
''<<print _args[0]>>'' · <<print _args[1]>> / <<print _args[2]>>
<</widget>>

! The guest beneath the stairs

CELLAR / SUGARCAST PASSAGE

The brass key opens a door disguised as wallpaper. Below it, the cellar is warm
with furnace breath. Jars of summer peaches glow on the shelves like captured
sunsets.

At the foot of the stairs crouches a shape in Mara's oldest quilt. It has no face,
only a hollow filled with slow-turning stars. Three black thorns pin its shadow to
the floor.

<<comfortMeter "THORNS REMAINING" $enemy.hp $enemy.maxHp>>

<<if not $hasKey>>
The hidden latch will not open. The scent of tea drifts from the entrance hall.

[[Return to the entrance for the key->Start]]
<<else>>
  <<if $enemy.hp > 0>>
The thing flinches when you move closer. This is not a guard. This is a guest who
has forgotten how to knock.

<<button "Offer one ordinary kindness">>
  <<set $enemy.hp -= 1>>
  <<set $warmth += 1>>
  <<set $log.push({id: $log.length, text: "A black thorn loosened when you spoke gently to the cellar guest."})>>
<</button>>
  <<else>>
> ''THE CELLAR GUEST''
> “Above the roof, my older self is dreaming. Please wake it softly. It frightens
> easily, and it is larger than your moon.”

The empty face fills, for an instant, with the reflection of a child asleep beside
a stove. It points toward the observatory.

[[Climb to the listening room->Observatory]]

[[Read the field notes->FieldNotes]]
  <</if>>
<</if>>

[[Return to the entrance->Start]]
